{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["And more. Beware of making books — like <i>take heed to yourselves</i> (the sense of) making. [There is] no end to them. As for למ״ד: it is a root like כלמ״ד. למד דעת — its weight is like the flaming sword, and it has no parallel. In the language of Ishmael it is like קריאה [reading]."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is compressed and elliptical. 'כמשקל להט החרב' likely refers to Genesis 3:24; the exact syntactic relationship of 'למד דעת' to what precedes is unclear. The reference to Ishmaelite (Arabic) 'קריאה' appears to explain למ״ד as equivalent to Arabic qirāʾa (reading/recitation). 'ואין לה דומה' may mean the Arabic word has no Hebrew cognate, or that למ״ד itself has no parallel form."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:26.068426272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}